WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.569
- So, my ego can fuel me,
but it can also destroy me.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:06.172
But I have the right tools in place and
the right people around me to make sure I,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.541
yeah, I stay grounded.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.275
- Balance.
- Balance.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.610
The duality of it.
- Mmhmm.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.513
So, you know, I know I'm the s--t,
but I know I ain’t s--t.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.506
Feels like it, with the baby grand piano.
- What’s up?

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.141
What's up, Taylor?

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:41.608
How are you?

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.842
- I'm great.
- You’re well?
- I'm sorry if

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.912
this walk-in is not as cool as your,
like, entrances—

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.414
- [Laughing] Nah, it’s still
a grand entrance.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.248
- To your fights.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.449
- Yeah, it's still a grand entrance.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.918
Yeah, we tried to mimic it as much as possible.
- That was good.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.220
- But it’s—
- I’m sure they’ll add, like, the background music as well.
- Absolutely.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.389
What song would you play?
- Oooh, right now?

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.859
“Cooped Up/Return of the Mack” remix.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.761
It's like a, it’s a dope remix. Yeah.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.030
- “Return of the Mack”—
- And “Cooped Up,” yeah.
- That's quite a pull.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:04.998
- OK.
- Yeah,

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:08.301
you know, I was about to say, Post Malone’s “Cooped Up,”
and then they juxtapose it with that.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.070
It was beautiful.
- A bit of a mashup.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.939
- Yeah.
- OK, I'mma add it to my playlist.
- Yeah.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:17.510
- OK, so speaking of music, you have never seen
or met me, but I actually have seen you.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.812
I just didn’t meet you.
- Mmhmm.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.213
- I was at Drake's house.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.916
- No way! Fuck off.
- Yeah, OVO Fest.
- Yeah.
- I saw you.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:23.750
- Damn.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.820
And I was like, “Wait, is that—”
- At the Embassy.
- Yes! And, OK—

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.056
- Yeah.
- How blown away were you about
how that house just transforms?

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.357
- I'm literally like—I didn’t

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.992
even know we were on the court.
- Yeah.
- I didn't know we were on the

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:33.760
basketball court till

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.330
I looked up. Like, my security was like,
“Look up,” and they see the hoops

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:41.367
folded up and then, yeah,
just seeing everyone around.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.102
Even—what’s his name?—

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.504
LeBron pulled up on me
and we talked for, like, a minute, 20,

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.305
and just—
- Yeah.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.074
- I was just—cuz I was expecting it—
I wasn't expecting to see him.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:52.011
So, that one kinda got me. Like,
oh, shit, did that just happen? Yeah.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.813
- Yeah. Just chillin’ at the house.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.048
- Yeah, I know. It's crazy.
- Yeah.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.852
So, for you, you’re, first off, at Drake's house—
- Mmhmm.
- And LeBron

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.821
James comes up to you at Drake's
house, knows you.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.990
- Mmhmm.
- What does he say?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.959
- It's hard to remember
cuz it was all in a moment.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.795
But we were just sharing love
pretty much for about a minute, 10.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:13.399
Just, like, showing love and appreciation
and, yeah, admiration for each other's work.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.234
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.237
And, yeah, I just gave him a dap-up
and then kept it moving.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.071
- Yeah.
- Mmhmm.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.774
- Something that I thought was really interesting and cool—
- Yeah.
- About you

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.877
being at Drake's
house is I've seen some interviews

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.880
where you talk about there
not being a lot of people

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.016
in the world that exist that can relate
to the position that you're in.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.351
- Mmhmm.
- And I would think

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:36.222
Drake is one of the few humans that do understand it—
- Yeah.
- On some level.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.724
- On a different level.
- Yeah.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.959
- Like, there's levels to that shit,
you know what I mean?

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:40.894
There's levels to this shit.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:44.264
Like, there was a, there was a video
I've seen of him

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.833
years ago in Melbourne
walking through the airport.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.602
I can understand why he has
Air Drake now.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.005
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah. Cuz there's levels to this.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.707
- Yeah. You would have to shut down
the entire airport.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:59.579
- Pretty much. The whole airport was just following him.
- Yeah.
- So, yeah. He can relate, but, again, there’s levels.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.747
- Yeah.
- Yeah.
- Absolutely.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:03.149
But, you know,
I do think there's something to, you know,

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:07.086
he is somebody who has always been
inspiring to me as a friend, as an artist,

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:11.624
because he became the things
that he wanted to become.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:15.528
And it's very hard to do that
and accomplish that, and I'm

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.598
sure in some ways, you're like,
“I had a path for myself

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.968
that I envisioned—”
- Yup.
- “And up to this point, I have reached it.”

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.269
- Mmhmm.
- Do you feel that way?

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:27.040
- I've reached it and exceeded it,
but there's other little things

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.709
that I still have to, you know,

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.845
attain. Like, different plateaus
I still have to get to.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:36.749
So, like, even two days ago,
I—what was the name of the building

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.385
we were at? The tall—
- [Offscreen:] One Vanderbilt.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:43.323
- One Vanderbilt. We were up there,
and I met Michael, who was the head

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.791
honcho of the whole place.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.558
And as I was there,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.528
I had a moment of, like, gratitude.
Just like, look where I'm at right now.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.796
I could see the whole of New York.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.864
And then there was fireworks
in Central Park.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.833
It was like
it was just right there for me.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.168
- Yeah.
- That's my ego.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:55.969
But, yeah,

00:03:55.969 --> 00:04:00.940
so for me, I was just, like, grateful.
Just a moment of gratitude and just really—

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.309
cuz everyone was just watching
cuz there's cameras all around

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.311
me and whatnot. I'm just like, man,
this is some cool shit.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.247
- Yeah
- But all right, we keep climbing.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:07.880
- Absolutely.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.084
And yet you said, so, there's, like,
different levels that you wanna attain.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:14.220
I almost think about it like a video game,
you know? You're, like, beating the boss.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.888
- I’ve been saying, I’m Player 1!
- Really?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.558
- Oh, like, last time I
flew to New York, to UFC 230,

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:22.061
I said, “I'm Player 1 in this shit
and everyone else is just kinda like

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.062
bots in my game.”

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.064
But I feel like everyone
should have that view of themselves

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.966
cuz you are the Player 1
in your own life.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.401
- Absolutely.
- Mm.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.704
- So, something I've always thought
is interesting, and it's one of the reasons

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.506
I'm really excited to
dive into this conversation is

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.842
I think
there are two occupations of people:

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.345
They can literally do whatever they want.
- Yep.
- And I think it's rappers

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.414
and fighters. You almost have no rules.
- Rappers and fighters.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.682
Not no rules,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.952
but I'll tell you one thing. Even, like,
when I walked into the Embassy, right?

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.321
I never play on this, but

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.391
when a football player walks in a

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.258
room, there’s

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:55.495
like, “Oh, shit, there's that guy.”
When a rapper walks in, there’s that guy.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:59.032
Even in a room full of rappers
and basketball players and football

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.934
players, when a fighter walks in a room,
it’s a different vibe.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:06.239
Cuz men,
we have testosterone and our ego.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.275
Everyone wants to be that guy
that can hold his own.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.680
But the difference is, everyone knows
I can hold my own, but I never play on it.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.614
I'm still very soft.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:18.051
I'm still very nice and respectful.
But I've seen guys, even rappers,

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:20.887
I've seen them walk around,
you know, like, just—

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.689
Like,
you know, like they boutta start some shit.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:26.259
And I don't walk around with that kind of ego
cuz I feel like—even I posted a clip

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:29.162
yesterday of Jordan Peterson talking about
being capable of being dangerous

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.031
but also being able to control it.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.234
Cuz if you're not a dangerous man
and you’re just like, “Oh, you know,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:39.405
I don't hurt anyone. I'm a nice guy.”
It's like your virtue is useless.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:42.375
It has no merit because
you have no capability of being dangerous.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.278
So, for me, when I walk in a room—
I notice it as well

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.480
when Mike Tyson—amongst fighters,

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.381
amongst fighters,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.818
when Mike Tyson walks in a room, everyone
just—boom.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.554
That's Mike Tyson.
- Yeah.
- That's Mike Tyson.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:57.223
But same thing. He never plays on it.
He's just,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.893
“Hey, man, how you doin’?” Like, you know, he's
real soft and chill, and he's older now.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:03.663
Maybe when he was younger—
- Mmhmm.
- He’d play on that shit. But me right now—

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.898
- I think definitely when he was younger.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.534
Oh, no, definitely he did. You know,
walking with a tiger and all that.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.803
- Yeah, but for me, I'm still,
I just chill. And I could notice

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.505
at the Embassy that peoples was—

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.973
cuz I didn't really follow basketball
like that.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.509
So, a lot of them were showing love
and whatnot.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:19.879
There was only one exception was
when, his house, Drake walked through,

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:23.583
and when LeBron was walking around,
then it's like, “Oh, shit, those are greats walkin’ around.”

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.518
- Both of them.
- Right, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:29.989
- So, were you always able to control it,
and how do you control it?

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:30.890
- That’s a good question.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.860
I wasn't always to control—

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.828
when you say “control it,” control
is as in—

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.096
- Well, you just referred to, like,

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.931
you know, there's something in being
dangerous, but also being able to—

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:39.298
- Oh, yeah.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.934
Yeah, definitely. Martial arts teaches you that.
- Yeah.
- Martial arts,

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.270
cuz there's also people who can't control it.
- Mmhmm.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:47.407
- And it's unfortunate, man,
cuz, like, you know,

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.778
I never got to even—
I don't know him like that.

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:54.480
But when I, when I
saw the news about Takeoff,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.216
it hurt me because I was like,
that was senseless.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.652
And that's
because now we're kinda finding out.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.620
We don't know the whole story yet.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.955
So, RIP to Takeoff and I
don't want to speak too much on that.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.624
But whatever his situation, all these

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:08.027
all these young rappers that are dying,
it seems like it just happens to be

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:12.598
our men who aren't emotionally intelligent
or understand their own feelings.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:15.701
So they just react, you know,
they see some shit.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.270
I have my own story about this.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.039
At the Justin Bieber thing,
a rapper tried to pull up on me

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.642
and I just let him know, like, "I'm
not about that life. I'm chillin', bro."

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.011
- Mmhmm.
- Like, he a little bit sly.

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:28.214
But yeah, my security, I tell you,
I was just like, "You don't want this."

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.683
[Laughing]
- Really? OK.
You don't need to go, like, deep into it.

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:33.119
When you say pull up on you,
it's like, why? Just...

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:34.754
- I think is he knew who

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:37.723
I was and he tried to say like, you know,
"You and my security should spar."

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:38.424
I was like, "What?"

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:43.095
- [Both laughing]
I'mma say that sounds like some
rapper shit, I'll say that.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:43.696
Yeah, I was like, "What do you mean?"

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.399
And then I was like, "Bro,
this is not what you want." Like...
- Yeah.

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:49.535
- And I said it in the nicest way possible,
but I think it's the same thing.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:52.638
His ego, because he wants to test my gangster.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.307
So I'm like, "I don't need it."

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:56.375
Google me, YouTube me, you'll see it.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.678
- You can watch me do it.
- Exactly.

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:01.581
- Well, separate from that,
what role has ego played in your life?

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:03.916
- Good and bad.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:09.288
When I was younger, I had to learn how to
manage my ago, because everyone has an ego.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.824
- Yeah.
- But you have to have a healthy ego.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:12.558
So for me,

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:16.429
I had to learn how to control it
in a sense where I make sure it doesn't,

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.831
cuz there's times in my life
when it's overtaking me

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.701
and made me look stupid,
and I cringe at those times.

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:24.570
But then I've learned from those and
I make sure I don't let that happen again.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.406
So my ego can fuel me,
but it can also destroy me.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:31.010
But I have the right tools in place and
the right people around me to make sure I,

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.046
Yeah, I stay grounded.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:34.614
Excuse me.

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:38.851
- Yeah, because I think ego
in some ways can also be a positive tool

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:41.153
because sometimes wanting to protect that

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:45.224
ego and can also,
I think, fuel you forward as well.
- 100 percent. Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:47.260
- So it's just kind of learning
that, that balance.
- Balance.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.594
The duality of it.

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:51.497
- So, you know, I know I'm the shit,
but I know I ain't shit.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.166
- I'mma steal that.
- Yeah. Nah, straight up.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:57.436
I know I walk around like I know
who the fuck I am. I know I'm the shit.

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:02.241
But at the same time, when I meet someone
new. Like example, people sometimes get

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:05.912
like, if their friend, their group of five
people, maybe four of them know who I am.

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:07.747
One person doesn't know who I am.

00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:09.782
They like, "Oh, I'm sorry.
I don't know who you are."

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:12.118
I'm like, "It's OK." I'm meeting you
for the first time as well.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.420
I like meeting people
who don't know who I am

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:18.291
because they have no preconceived
notion of what they think of me.

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:21.027
They haven't seen me on TV
or maybe they haven't studied me

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.529
or watched me in interviews
or shit like that. So they don't,

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:26.799
they get to meet me for the first time
as me, rather than with the idea

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:28.334
of who they think I am.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.870
- Mmhmm.
- I actually, I appreciate that
when people don't know who I am,

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:33.506
I don't appreciate what people know,
who I am, and they pretend not to.

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:35.675
That's another story.
- Yeah, and that's also just weird.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:36.909
- Yeah. I'm like, "What the fuck?"

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:39.211
I see you. I know you, like, you fu... like why

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.513
you pretending like you don't care?

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.949
- Yeah.
- I'm like, just be cool. Yeah.
- [Laughs].

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:45.151
Someone told me this quote once,
a long time ago.

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:50.089
They said, "I'm not who I think I am
and I'm not who you think I am.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:55.294
I'm who I think you think I am."
- Ooo. Break that down.
- Essentially saying that...

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:56.329
- Let me, let me... break that down.

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:59.832
- Sometimes we adapt who

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:03.269
we are based on what we know
that person thinks of us.

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:05.805
So it's almost like a self-fulfilling
prophecy, right?
- Yeah.

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:11.911
- Like, if someone is expecting you to be
Israel Adesanya, you kind of become that.

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:12.945
- I'll tell you a story.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:16.382
So before my first title
defense in Melbourne,

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:19.485
biggest show ever. That fight week
or the week before that fight week,

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:22.188
I had an epiphany in myself
on my way home from training.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:26.959
I realized when I meet fans
I don't have to match the energy,

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.629
cuz normally—same thing—

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:34.533
I'd meet a fan back then and when they're,
"Oh my God, Israel!" Even if I'm, like,

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:38.638
maybe just cooling at a two, not a 10,
and they come at me with a 10,

00:10:39.005 --> 00:10:44.610
I'll raise my energy up to match theirs
just so I can be who they think I am.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.078
I'm like, I'm just chilling, bro.

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:50.116
I'm having a sandwich, I'm doing whatever,
pumping gas.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.885
"I'm such a big fan [grumbling]."

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:54.053
And I'm just like, "Yeah [sighs]."

00:10:54.053 --> 00:10:56.555
And I have to raise my energy up
and give them the whole song and dance

00:10:57.523 --> 00:10:58.124
just to make sure.

00:10:58.124 --> 00:11:00.292
- But then you're like, "Do I have to?" Like, you reach a...
- No, no.

00:11:00.292 --> 00:11:02.762
- Yeah.
- I had that epiphany,
and I was just like, "I don't have to."

00:11:02.762 --> 00:11:05.898
So now if someone comes at me at a 10.
After that fight week,

00:11:05.898 --> 00:11:09.168
so after that fight itself,
I was going back to the airport,

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:10.770
I was going to the airport to go back
home.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.538
And I remember putting out a story saying

00:11:12.538 --> 00:11:14.607
like, look,
because I remember I was just tapped out.

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:16.275
All my energy was, my bandwidth

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:18.344
I had none for external shit.

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:22.481
So I said, If you see me on the streets
or if you see me at the airport,

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:25.918
please don't come at me running or yelling
because I'll walk away.

00:11:26.452 --> 00:11:27.253
I put that up.

00:11:27.253 --> 00:11:30.823
I was just I just don't want to deal
with, like, the energy.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:32.091
So people actually approached me.

00:11:32.091 --> 00:11:34.860
People saw my story,
and they were like, "Hey, Israel.

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:36.829
So I'm a big fan. Would you mind?"

00:11:36.829 --> 00:11:40.866
And I'm like, "Oh, yeah, easy ask." Because
they respected my, my, my boundaries.

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:42.702
And that's the thing.
You have to protect your boundaries.

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:47.373
And sometimes fans get entitled and think
like they... I'm like, "I don't give a fuck.

00:11:47.606 --> 00:11:49.041
I don't know who you are."
- Right.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.209
- You know who I am, yes.

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:52.445
But this is historic for you.

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:54.013
This is just regular for me.

00:11:54.013 --> 00:11:55.081
- Absolutely.
- Yeah.

00:11:55.081 --> 00:11:57.016
- And if you don't, like, follow that.

00:11:57.016 --> 00:11:59.819
- Oh, you're an asshole.
- There's you're drained, there's burn out.

00:11:59.819 --> 00:12:02.955
- No, I'm saying you feel like, "OK,
I have to be." You will get burned out.

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:03.923
- I gotta look after me first.

00:12:03.923 --> 00:12:06.459
- [Both:] Yeah
- I look after me first.
- Absolutely.

00:12:06.759 --> 00:12:07.993
You know, in a lot of interviews

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:12.431
that I've watched of you,
something that comes up a lot is you,

00:12:12.431 --> 00:12:15.367
I guess, not feeling attached to things.
Like, whether that people's

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:17.670
comments of you,
whether it's your title belt.

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:19.839
So what are you attached to?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.641
- What am I attached to? Ooo,

00:12:22.641 --> 00:12:25.778
that's a good, man, this is going deep.
- [Both laughing.]

00:12:25.945 --> 00:12:28.047
- Welcome to the show!
- [Both laughing.]

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.416
- What am I attached to?

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:32.918
Yeah, um...

00:12:32.918 --> 00:12:33.552
fuck.

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:35.554
This is something I learned from Avatar
as well.

00:12:35.554 --> 00:12:38.791
The show, which my nickname comes from.

00:12:40.092 --> 00:12:40.760
- Yes, The Airbender, I know.
- Yeah.

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.795
When he met Guru Pathik

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:46.532
and he had to learn how to detach himself
from worldly possessions

00:12:46.532 --> 00:12:49.301
because he wanted to be able
to control the Avatar state.

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:53.773
There was seven chakras he had to unlock,
and one of them was detachment.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.076
The hardest one for him was to
detach from Katara.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:00.146
But for me, what am I attached to?

00:13:00.146 --> 00:13:03.949
I guess my family, first of all,
because they will always be there.

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:06.385
They've been there before
all of this happened.

00:13:06.385 --> 00:13:07.920
They've been there before all this.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.121
So they will always be there.

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:11.690
So I'm attached to them.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:14.026
My dogs, I keep them with me.
- Love that.

00:13:15.828 --> 00:13:17.663
- I'm attached to them.

00:13:17.663 --> 00:13:20.266
And my,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:21.400
uh, my gym,

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:26.071
yes. My training, my training,
my values in that space.

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.140
But yeah, any material things?

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.109
I'm not really attached
to. Material things

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:31.310
I'm not, I love them.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.279
Don't get me wrong, I like to fucking floss.

00:13:33.279 --> 00:13:36.282
I'm light right now
- [Laughing]
- But yeah, I like to flex,

00:13:36.282 --> 00:13:38.884
but I'm not attached to those things.
I don't, like,

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.820
they don't define me. I make them.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:41.687
They don't make me.
- Mmhmm,

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:45.558
but I wanna know if you had seven chakras
what they would be?

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:47.426
If you titled them,
or do you already know?
- No.

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:48.761
Everyone has seven chakras.

00:13:48.761 --> 00:13:49.528
But if I had seven chakras.

00:13:49.528 --> 00:13:51.931
- I'm saying ones that you
personalize, like these are like.
- Oh,

00:13:52.264 --> 00:13:53.766
OK, damn OK, that's [clicks teeth].

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.768
- But we'll come back to it.
Just ruminate on it.
- Yeah, I'mma have to.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:56.602
Yeah, OK. Bet. Bet.

00:13:56.769 --> 00:14:01.674
- But on that subject of detachment
leads me to obviously there's

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:05.311
this clip that always goes viral of you.
- Yeah.
- Solo shot.

00:14:05.945 --> 00:14:08.581
It's just you, and you're saying, "I'm
prepared."

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:09.949
- Oh, yeah, every fight week.

00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:12.785
I love that. I love that for me.
- It's you saying, "I'm prepared.

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:14.253
I'm prepared to die."

00:14:15.287 --> 00:14:16.388
- Mmhmm.
- Did you mean that?

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:18.824
- Yes. I honestly, people think it's some...

00:14:19.325 --> 00:14:21.594
I'm in the fight for my life
in that moment.

00:14:21.727 --> 00:14:22.061
OK.

00:14:22.061 --> 00:14:24.630
So, the fight itself,
I'll—you need to watch.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.731
I'll send it to you.

00:14:25.731 --> 00:14:28.834
But, like, the first round, it's
my title fight, right?

00:14:28.834 --> 00:14:31.270
I'm about to become the UFC champion.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:33.005
The first round, I get rocked,

00:14:33.005 --> 00:14:35.207
and it's the first time
I've ever been rocked in a UFC fight.

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:39.011
And then I remember the arena
erupting, like, "Holy s--t, this is it.

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.046
The hype train is about to be exposed.

00:14:41.046 --> 00:14:42.748
He's about to"—you know how people get.

00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:44.950
- And then went back to my corner.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.953
So, I lost that first round,
and I was like, "It's okay, I'll regroup."

00:14:47.953 --> 00:14:49.255
I never lost focus.

00:14:49.255 --> 00:14:51.257
Second round, I drop him.

00:14:51.257 --> 00:14:54.593
Third round, I style on him.
Fourth round, I'm whuppin' his ass.

00:14:54.593 --> 00:14:57.763
And then he makes a calculated chess move,
and he hasn't thrown a head

00:14:57.763 --> 00:15:02.167
kick the whole fight, and he catches
me. Boom. Hits me in the head,

00:15:02.167 --> 00:15:06.272
and I'm there. Takes him about maybe three,
four seconds to realize I'm rocked.

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:07.873
Then he tries to hurt me,

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:10.609
tries to finish me,
and then he took that round.

00:15:10.609 --> 00:15:12.244
So, we're 2-2
going into the fifth round,

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:16.081
the last round. I made the
agreement with myself in my own

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:16.749
soul, like,

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:18.851
if this is how I

00:15:18.851 --> 00:15:22.154
die, trying to attain this,
what a glorious death.

00:15:22.721 --> 00:15:24.189
So, I signed my life away.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:27.359
I literally—my parents were in the crowd,
my family was in the crowd.

00:15:27.359 --> 00:15:29.728
But I signed my life away, like,

00:15:29.728 --> 00:15:31.063
if this is how I go, this is how I go,

00:15:31.063 --> 00:15:33.132
but what a way to die.
What a way to go out.

00:15:33.132 --> 00:15:34.600
But guess what?

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.970
If I'm prepared to die,
I'm prepared to kill.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.040
So, in that fifth round, I found a new

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.910
level to my fighting spirit that
I never knew was there.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.478
I tapped into it, and I was just—

00:15:46.478 --> 00:15:49.181
I looked like I was fresh
from the first round, and I dropped—

00:15:49.181 --> 00:15:51.417
It was the most knockdowns
in a title fight.

00:15:51.417 --> 00:15:53.452
I dropped him so many times
in that last round,

00:15:53.786 --> 00:15:56.922
and I almost finished him at the end.
Like, literally maybe another three seconds,

00:15:56.922 --> 00:15:57.623
it would have been over.

00:15:57.623 --> 00:16:00.960
But the time ran out, and the referee
pulled me off him and saved him.

00:16:01.427 --> 00:16:02.428
- Yeah.
- But, yeah, I meant that.

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:03.629
I really meant that because,

00:16:03.629 --> 00:16:06.131
wow, what a glorious
moment that would be.

00:16:06.699 --> 00:16:11.070
- So as weird as this is to say,
what I'm kind of gathering is, like,

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:16.842
there was actually some freedom
in being prepared to die.

00:16:17.142 --> 00:16:19.211
- Not everybody dies,
but not everybody lives.

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:21.447
Or is it? No, everybody dies,
but not everybody lives.

00:16:21.947 --> 00:16:24.350
- Mmhmm.
- That's that bar right there,
cuz a lot of people,

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:28.387
they don't really get to live
because they're too sheltered.

00:16:28.387 --> 00:16:30.456
They don't really go
out of their comfort zone.

00:16:30.456 --> 00:16:35.527
So, for me, I was forced to live and, yeah,
I showed them how I can live.

00:16:35.561 --> 00:16:36.195
- Yeah.

00:16:36.195 --> 00:16:39.565
Cuz I mean, you do understand,
like, the weight of that sentence.

00:16:39.565 --> 00:16:39.898
- Yeah.

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:42.434
- Like, "I am prepared to die."
- It was—

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:43.302
I didn't plan it.

00:16:43.302 --> 00:16:45.738
It was just in the moment.
- Yeah.
- I looked at him, I said, "You're not gonna beat me.

00:16:45.771 --> 00:16:47.306
I'm prepared to die."

00:16:47.306 --> 00:16:49.808
And I said in my native tongue in Yoruba,
I said, "Ayabiekun,"

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:51.477
and that's like, “The heart of a lion.”

00:16:51.477 --> 00:16:53.379
And we just went at it.

00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:54.947
- Yeah.
- Yeah, I took him out then.

00:16:54.947 --> 00:16:58.851
- So, then what did it feel like
to get to the other side of that win

00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:01.020
and not have to die to do it?
- Yeah.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.890
- Yeah.
- For me, just the—when I was, like,
I remember, um, the referee was holding

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:05.290
my hand.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.761
Cuz they hold your hand and are like, "Aaaand new—"

00:17:08.761 --> 00:17:10.863
And I was just, like,
"Please don't f--k me over.

00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:12.097
I know I won this fight."

00:17:12.097 --> 00:17:14.633
And then when they raised my hand—
every time I watch that fight back,

00:17:15.401 --> 00:17:16.335
I look at myself.

00:17:16.335 --> 00:17:18.437
I'm, like, listening, listening. "Israel."

00:17:19.304 --> 00:17:22.541
And my hands went up, and I just had
the sense of, like, yes, thank you.

00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:25.044
But then you look at
him, and I remember his face. "Ugh."

00:17:26.345 --> 00:17:28.147
And forever I'm gonna be grateful

00:17:28.147 --> 00:17:31.717
that, you know—shout out to Kelvin Gastelum.
He's a formidable opponent.

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:36.889
He brought the best out of me, um,
but his head going down, that was just—

00:17:36.889 --> 00:17:39.958
I'm glad that wasn't me that night,
cuz to go through that fire

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:44.563
and not get the gold, that—I woulda been fine.

00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:46.165
Don't get me wrong,
I'll definitely get over it.

00:17:46.165 --> 00:17:48.434
I've gotten over
worse things in my life, but

00:17:48.434 --> 00:17:50.969
whenever I see that moment,
I'm always glad my hand got raised.

00:17:51.103 --> 00:17:51.870
- Yeah. Absolutely.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.139
- There was a sense of relief, like, "Yes,
we did it."

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:58.610
I set a goal for myself
before I even knew I was a great fighter.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.312
I just knew I would be.
Oh, I didn't, you just—

00:18:00.312 --> 00:18:01.647
Ali said it: "I'm the greatest.

00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:03.248
I said it before I knew I was."

00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:05.551
- Yeah.
- You know, and I just knew, like,
there's something in me.

00:18:05.551 --> 00:18:06.718
You have it. You just know.

00:18:06.718 --> 00:18:08.787
- Yeah.
- So, I'm glad I attained that that day.
And just [clicking tongue].

00:18:09.421 --> 00:18:10.589
That's one off the list.

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:13.992
- Mmhmm. And I mean, just iconic moment,
that clip is, like—
- Iconic. Yes.

00:18:14.093 --> 00:18:15.427
- Wild.
- Yeah.

00:18:15.427 --> 00:18:18.163
- Do you think that just as a fighter,
you have to compartmentalize

00:18:18.163 --> 00:18:19.064
