- Yeah.

00:30:36.601 --> 00:30:38.870
- And the same thing even with this guy
that I'm fighting next weekend.

00:30:38.870 --> 00:30:39.838
He's knocked me

00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:43.641
out in the previous, like, five years ago
in kickboxing. But same again.

00:30:43.741 --> 00:30:45.910
I never, look at me now.
- Mmhmm.

00:30:46.010 --> 00:30:48.780
- He's beaten me supposedly twice,
but look at me now. I'm the one winning.

00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:51.983
And he kept on trying to get at me
because I'm doing so much

00:30:51.983 --> 00:30:52.884
better than him in life.

00:30:52.884 --> 00:30:55.420
- Yeah. So defeat isn't, like, a thing that

00:30:55.720 --> 00:30:58.122
happens to you. It's something you feel.
- You accept this.

00:30:58.389 --> 00:31:00.391
Yeah, you accept defeat. Some people, in life,

00:31:00.658 --> 00:31:03.094
there's times in life
I felt defeated away from fighting.

00:31:03.328 --> 00:31:03.995
- Yeah.

00:31:03.995 --> 00:31:08.333
- Life kicked my ass.
Like, 2013 was my great depression.

00:31:08.333 --> 00:31:09.634
I remember that year. It was,

00:31:09.634 --> 00:31:11.302
I was, that's when I moved to China.

00:31:11.302 --> 00:31:14.339
I quit my job September 4th, 2013.

00:31:14.339 --> 00:31:16.474
That was my last 9 to 5.
September 5th,

00:31:16.474 --> 00:31:18.509
I was on a plane to China.
And I tried to quit that job

00:31:18.509 --> 00:31:19.844
three times prior.

00:31:19.844 --> 00:31:23.915
But that time I got it right, and I set
everything up so I can
just [clapping] out of there.

00:31:23.915 --> 00:31:26.751
But it was because
life made me really uncomfortable.

00:31:26.751 --> 00:31:29.220
Life put me in a place that I...

00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:31.890
Yeah, it was really bad.
So I was defeated.

00:31:31.890 --> 00:31:36.694
But then I, again, you can dust yourself
up, rise back up and get what's yours.

00:31:36.694 --> 00:31:38.196
- How did you get out of that place?

00:31:39.197 --> 00:31:40.265
- Mentality.

00:31:40.265 --> 00:31:44.302
The mentality I had. And for me,
the key people around me. The key people

00:31:44.302 --> 00:31:47.438
I had around me as well. But I think it
was just my spirit, my fighting spirit.

00:31:47.438 --> 00:31:50.508
And also a lot of prayers
from mom and dad, my spiritual warriors.

00:31:50.508 --> 00:31:52.744
You know? Yeah, they help me a lot.

00:31:52.744 --> 00:31:53.478
- I love that.

00:31:53.478 --> 00:31:56.881
- Mm.
- OK, I am going to say some words.

00:31:56.915 --> 00:31:57.515
- All right, shoot.

00:31:57.615 --> 00:32:01.920
- And I want you to tell me either
the role they play in your life,
- Mmhmm.

00:32:02.086 --> 00:32:05.657
- what emotion
you know, elicits, like, what happens

00:32:05.657 --> 00:32:08.293
when you hear them.
OK?
- OK.
- Revenge.

00:32:09.327 --> 00:32:12.063
- ♪♪♪ Looking for revenge. ♪♪♪

00:32:12.063 --> 00:32:14.599
- All summer 16.

00:32:14.966 --> 00:32:17.435
- Eh, on November 12th, eh.
On November 12th, uh.

00:32:17.969 --> 00:32:19.671
Revenge. Revenge.

00:32:19.938 --> 00:32:22.173
There's so many things about revenge.

00:32:22.173 --> 00:32:24.509
And it's not always the best option.

00:32:25.510 --> 00:32:27.011
There's a time for revenge.

00:32:27.011 --> 00:32:28.546
I never went looking for this fight.

00:32:28.546 --> 00:32:30.949
Like I said,
- Mmhmm.
- I let it go a long time ago.

00:32:31.316 --> 00:32:33.451
I'm just living my life, being great.

00:32:33.451 --> 00:32:35.687
And then life presented me
with this opportunity.
- Mmhmm.

00:32:36.387 --> 00:32:38.489
- Cuz I was patient,
and I didn't go looking for it.

00:32:38.489 --> 00:32:40.258
It's like, here. Now it's yours.

00:32:40.258 --> 00:32:42.360
Take it. I'm like, aight.

00:32:42.360 --> 00:32:43.928
So now it's time for revenge.

00:32:43.928 --> 00:32:46.431
But you can't go looking for it
constantly.

00:32:46.597 --> 00:32:49.233
I don't think, like, that's the best thing.
Cuz, again, you're in that mindset.

00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:50.902
You might

00:32:51.035 --> 00:32:53.738
spray the wrong people
sometimes if you're in that mindset

00:32:53.738 --> 00:32:56.341
all the time. Not,
you know, like, physically

00:32:56.341 --> 00:32:59.210
but, like, emotionally
and snap at the wrong people.

00:32:59.477 --> 00:33:01.946
Cuz I know people who stay
in that mindset, and they just, like,

00:33:02.447 --> 00:33:04.349
they burn bridges a lot.
- Yeah.
- A lot.

00:33:04.349 --> 00:33:07.785
So, yeah, revenge plays a good
role in life, but you have to know when to

00:33:08.119 --> 00:33:09.620
look for revenge.

00:33:09.620 --> 00:33:11.089
And again, what did I say?

00:33:11.089 --> 00:33:12.690
I said: God forgives. I don't.

00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.393
The Lord said vengeance is mine.
And I'm like, yeah, me too.

00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:16.761
And now it's mine.

00:33:17.729 --> 00:33:18.963
- I love it.
You pull quotables.

00:33:18.963 --> 00:33:20.932
- I'm just freestyling.
- Yeah.

00:33:20.932 --> 00:33:23.067
OK, next word.
- Yeah.
- Violence.

00:33:23.201 --> 00:33:25.036
- Violence.

00:33:25.036 --> 00:33:26.637
Violence

00:33:27.305 --> 00:33:28.940
isn't always the answer.

00:33:28.940 --> 00:33:30.608
But again, there's a time for violence.

00:33:30.608 --> 00:33:32.010
And like I said,

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:35.913
you have to be capable of violence
as a person. Not just as a man.

00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:39.917
I feel like as a person. But as a man,
you have to be capable of violence.

00:33:39.917 --> 00:33:44.489
It's better to be a warrior
in a garden than a gardener in a war.

00:33:45.223 --> 00:33:48.326
Cuz, you know, when
it's time to get down, to get busy,

00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:52.397
I need to know I can take care of me
and my own, you know?

00:33:52.397 --> 00:33:54.365
So violence is necessary.

00:33:54.365 --> 00:33:56.100
Every man needs to learn martial arts.

00:33:56.100 --> 00:33:59.170
They need to put it in school
and teach them how to meditate as well.

00:33:59.470 --> 00:34:05.743
So you're capable of violence,
but you know how to, you know, keep cool.

00:34:06.177 --> 00:34:06.878
Yeah.

00:34:06.911 --> 00:34:07.245
- I like,

00:34:07.245 --> 00:34:10.415
I see, like, in a lot of your interviews,
you're like, I know how to speak violence.

00:34:10.415 --> 00:34:11.916
- I can.
- Yeah.

00:34:11.916 --> 00:34:15.720
- Like, also there's times in my life
when people have wronged me in the worst way,

00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:17.155
and I can get dark on them.
- Mmhmm.

00:34:18.356 --> 00:34:19.257
- I've said this.

00:34:19.257 --> 00:34:21.359
There's no, people try and be virtuous.

00:34:21.359 --> 00:34:24.228
Like I said, they say, "I'm a good person."
I'm like, you're not virtuous.

00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:25.930
You're only a good person
cuz you have to be.

00:34:25.930 --> 00:34:27.198
Cuz you can't do shit.
- Mmhmm.

00:34:27.265 --> 00:34:31.235
- It means nothing that you're a "good person"
cuz you're weak. That's why.

00:34:31.602 --> 00:34:35.006
But if you're a violent person like myself,
and I choose to be a good person to you,

00:34:35.006 --> 00:34:36.841
it means something.

00:34:36.841 --> 00:34:38.976
Cuz I could destroy you.
- Mmhmm.
- It's different.

00:34:39.177 --> 00:34:39.510
So if

00:34:39.510 --> 00:34:44.215
I'm violent, capable of violence,
but I'm virtuous in my goodness,

00:34:44.215 --> 00:34:46.484
then that's different.
So I say there's no good or bad people.

00:34:47.018 --> 00:34:49.720
People are just capable of great
good or great evil.

00:34:50.254 --> 00:34:51.856
We're human beings.

00:34:51.856 --> 00:34:53.057
There's a duality.

00:34:53.057 --> 00:34:56.260
So there's times I've been evil,
but there's a lot of times I'm good.

00:34:56.527 --> 00:34:59.397
- OK, next word.
- Mmhmm?
- Perfection.

00:34:59.697 --> 00:35:02.667
- Eh, not me.
I chase it in martial arts.

00:35:03.968 --> 00:35:05.970
I know I'll never attain it.

00:35:05.970 --> 00:35:09.507
But it's
the pursuit of perfection in my craft.

00:35:09.707 --> 00:35:13.744
- Yeah.
- In my artwork. In the way I live.

00:35:13.744 --> 00:35:15.546
But I just know perfection is,
I will never attain it.

00:35:15.546 --> 00:35:19.317
I never—cuz you grow up with that
kind of pressure a little bit sometimes.

00:35:19.317 --> 00:35:22.420
And certain, even people who are
always expecting that from me when I fight.

00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:25.690
Like, "He's gonna be perfect," this and that.
But I'm like, fuck your expectations.
- Mmhmm.

00:35:26.324 --> 00:35:27.525
- It's about my expectations.

00:35:27.525 --> 00:35:29.894
So, you can keep that over.
[Burping]

00:35:29.894 --> 00:35:30.328
Excuse me.

00:35:30.328 --> 00:35:31.562
You can keep that over there.

00:35:31.562 --> 00:35:34.332
- Yep. Last word.
- Mmhmm?
- Alex Pereira.

00:35:34.565 --> 00:35:37.902
- Alex Pereira.

00:35:37.902 --> 00:35:39.504
Mm, let me see.

00:35:40.838 --> 00:35:41.939
He's got a head like,

00:35:41.939 --> 00:35:44.542
you know, those Easter Island statues?

00:35:45.009 --> 00:35:47.411
- I do.
- Yeah. They call him Hands of Stone,

00:35:47.411 --> 00:35:48.713
but he's got a head of stone as well.

00:35:48.713 --> 00:35:51.682
And I know this, but I can break blocks.

00:35:52.650 --> 00:35:55.386
Yeah, I break bricks now.
- Mmhmm.

00:35:55.386 --> 00:35:59.190
You know, this is going to be a fun fight.
And there's a lot to dive into with it.

00:35:59.190 --> 00:36:03.494
So I think since we're here,
we might as well just start.
- [Whooshing sound]
- For you,

00:36:03.995 --> 00:36:07.598
- Mmhmm?
- what does this fight represent
specifically?
- For me,

00:36:07.598 --> 00:36:11.602
what does it represent?

00:36:11.602 --> 00:36:13.804
A chance to rewrite history.

00:36:13.804 --> 00:36:17.642
A chance to, I can't
change the past.

00:36:17.642 --> 00:36:19.677
It's happened.
That is the past. I've let it go.

00:36:20.211 --> 00:36:24.549
But now there's an opportunity
now to rewrite history for the future.

00:36:24.949 --> 00:36:26.751
This is my chance.
And that's why I've done it.

00:36:26.751 --> 00:36:31.656
Every single thing in my power
in this camp to make sure that happens.

00:36:32.056 --> 00:36:35.626
And I'm so confident. So much confidence
that my wrestling coach is like,

00:36:35.626 --> 00:36:38.029
"Yo, let's go play table
tennis. I'll humble you real quick."
- [Laughing]

00:36:38.462 --> 00:36:39.897
- Cuz they can see,

00:36:39.897 --> 00:36:42.266
they can see—oh, yesterday
after I trained, Tim, how was I?
Exactly.

00:36:43.334 --> 00:36:45.536
- Tim says...
- Savage.

00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:47.405
And I don't want to say too much
cuz people talk.

00:36:47.405 --> 00:36:50.208
You supposed to hype a fight up.
You think I'm coming in
like,

00:36:51.509 --> 00:36:52.510
I might do all right.

00:36:52.510 --> 00:36:54.111
You know what I'm saying?
Nah, Imma fuck this guy up.

00:36:54.111 --> 00:36:54.779
- Yeah.

00:36:54.779 --> 00:36:56.847
- But I don't want to say too much
cuz he's got bragging rights.
- Mmhmm.

00:36:57.181 --> 00:36:58.883
- And I understand that.
So I'm like, you know what,

00:36:58.883 --> 00:37:01.085
let him think whatever he wants.
Let him, it's all good.

00:37:01.085 --> 00:37:04.288
Eh, easy as, you know.

00:37:04.288 --> 00:37:07.491
- So with that being said
then, what is the difference,

00:37:07.491 --> 00:37:10.561
