a bit more than the other.

00:38:36.213 --> 00:38:37.348
And I'm not saying they care about it

00:38:37.348 --> 00:38:39.417
in the way
that's gonna, like, make them win.
- OK.

00:38:39.417 --> 00:38:43.754
- I'm saying they feel like winning
will mean more to them.

00:38:43.888 --> 00:38:45.156
- Mmhmm.

00:38:45.156 --> 00:38:49.126
- Do you feel like in this
there is somebody who

00:38:49.894 --> 00:38:52.463
winning is gonna be a bit more important?

00:38:52.897 --> 00:38:54.899
OK, explain.
- Me.

00:38:54.899 --> 00:38:57.268
Cuz, again, rewrite history.
- Mmhmm.

00:38:57.268 --> 00:38:59.637
- You know, this guy's beaten me.

00:38:59.637 --> 00:39:03.374
I've fucking pretty much cleaned out
the middleweight division, my division.

00:39:03.407 --> 00:39:06.077
That's why I went up to try and capture
the light heavyweight belt.

00:39:07.044 --> 00:39:08.479
But I'm going to lap the division again.

00:39:08.479 --> 00:39:09.980
I'm lapping them right now.

00:39:09.980 --> 00:39:10.748
I've cleared the way.

00:39:10.748 --> 00:39:12.850
So, without me, he wouldn't be here.

00:39:12.850 --> 00:39:15.519
- Yeah.
- He would've got exposed a long time ago.

00:39:15.720 --> 00:39:19.423
So he's pretty much blessed
to be in this opportunity.

00:39:20.391 --> 00:39:24.128
So I'm happy to, yeah, expose him
when it's time.

00:39:24.128 --> 00:39:26.263
But right now, I'm like, let people
watch the highlights.

00:39:26.263 --> 00:39:28.032
Let them think
what they want to think. And...
- Mmhmm.

00:39:28.032 --> 00:39:30.067
- Yeah. Time will tell.

00:39:30.668 --> 00:39:33.504
- What have you learned about yourself
in preparation for this fight?

00:39:34.739 --> 00:39:40.378
- Hmm. In the preparation for this fight...

00:39:40.378 --> 00:39:42.646
Hmm, what have I learned, what's something—
I already knew I'm a savage.

00:39:43.180 --> 00:39:45.950
I knew the levels I can go.

00:39:46.951 --> 00:39:50.154
My mental capability to endure.

00:39:51.088 --> 00:39:55.259
Yeah, I don't want to go too much into it,
but there's a lot of stuff that happens.

00:39:55.259 --> 00:39:57.528
You know, sometimes outside of the gym,
sometimes in the gym.

00:39:57.895 --> 00:40:00.765
But yeah.
Police. Why is the police here?

00:40:00.765 --> 00:40:02.099
Sorry.
- No, it's OK.

00:40:02.099 --> 00:40:03.467
- I'm Black, you know.

00:40:03.467 --> 00:40:04.001
- Oh, I get it.

00:40:04.001 --> 00:40:05.970
I'm like, police are here?

00:40:05.970 --> 00:40:07.204
- What the fuck are they here for?

00:40:07.838 --> 00:40:10.875
But yeah, uh, yeah, just

00:40:11.976 --> 00:40:14.311
my capacity to endure cuz,

00:40:16.080 --> 00:40:16.781
yeah.

00:40:16.847 --> 00:40:18.749
Heavy is the head that wears the crown.

00:40:18.749 --> 00:40:19.383
I got a big head,

00:40:19.383 --> 00:40:22.653
so I got a big crown.
- Yeah.
- And I can handle it.
- Yeah.

00:40:22.653 --> 00:40:23.687
And I think, you know,

00:40:23.687 --> 00:40:27.792
enduring things, that really is just, OK,
who is going to outlast the other?

00:40:28.259 --> 00:40:31.262
And that's most of everything.
So...
- You watch.

00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:32.897
- Yeah.
- You watch.
- I'll be watching. I'm ready.

00:40:32.897 --> 00:40:35.666
- Yeah, like,
I know for a fact I can outlast him.

00:40:35.900 --> 00:40:36.066
- Yeah.

00:40:36.100 --> 00:40:36.901
- So this is where

00:40:36.901 --> 00:40:39.136
that fortitude comes.
- Mmhmm.

00:40:39.136 --> 00:40:40.438
- That mental fortitude.

00:40:40.438 --> 00:40:41.705
And knowing who I am,

00:40:41.705 --> 00:40:45.176
knowing my spirit, my fighting spirit.
I'm not underestimating him.

00:40:45.509 --> 00:40:48.212
They tell you, "Never underestimate anyone."
But they forget to tell you,

00:40:48.212 --> 00:40:50.481
"Never overestimate them."

00:40:50.481 --> 00:40:52.583
- No, fear makes the wolf bigger than he is.
- Yeah.

00:40:52.583 --> 00:40:55.019
- I always say that.
- A lot of people just, they get,

00:40:55.319 --> 00:40:57.188
I'll show you a little secret right now.
Look at this.

00:40:57.188 --> 00:41:01.158
This is my background. This is my background
right now on my lockscreen.

00:41:01.158 --> 00:41:06.931
But then when you open it...hold up.
- Wow.
- Shh.

00:41:08.165 --> 00:41:09.800
- And so you see that every day?

00:41:09.800 --> 00:41:12.002
- Yeah. I did something last night
that kind of made me,

00:41:12.002 --> 00:41:13.137
I did, like, a little thing.

00:41:13.137 --> 00:41:15.806
I was like, huh.
So then now I changed it last night.

00:41:15.806 --> 00:41:18.676
So that way
when I opened this, I'm just like,

00:41:18.676 --> 00:41:20.010
interesting.
- Yeah.

00:41:20.010 --> 00:41:23.180
- Just to put it back in my psyche.
Just to put it in my forefront

00:41:23.180 --> 00:41:25.082
whenever I open my phone. Just to know.

00:41:25.082 --> 00:41:27.718
Just so I know.
- Yeah. What's possible.

00:41:27.885 --> 00:41:28.652
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:41:28.652 --> 00:41:29.487
- I can make him bleed.

00:41:29.487 --> 00:41:33.524
And I already said I'm gonna make this
a horror movie. But hey, man,

00:41:33.524 --> 00:41:35.726
sometimes people sleep
through horror movies, so

00:41:36.994 --> 00:41:39.163
stay tuned,
bring a pillow and enjoy the show.

00:41:39.630 --> 00:41:40.931
- [Laughing] No, I love that.

00:41:40.931 --> 00:41:41.232
OK,

00:41:41.232 --> 00:41:43.901
so generally,
not just focused on this fight,

00:41:43.901 --> 00:41:46.303
I want you to fill in the blank for me,
OK?

00:41:46.303 --> 00:41:49.073
I am the most blank fighter.

00:41:52.109 --> 00:41:55.980
- Ooh. I am the most

00:41:57.581 --> 00:41:59.450
intelligent fighter. Yeah.

00:41:59.450 --> 00:42:00.818
- Explain.

00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:03.320
- I think the way I look at the game.

00:42:03.320 --> 00:42:03.854
But that's me,

00:42:03.854 --> 00:42:05.990
I'm being biased because I'm me
and I think I'm really smart.

00:42:05.990 --> 00:42:08.859
But also I'm the most creative fighter.

00:42:08.859 --> 00:42:11.362
I've, in my own sense, changed the game.

00:42:12.296 --> 00:42:13.931
But it's not just me, it's my team.

00:42:13.931 --> 00:42:16.367
The way we played the striking game,
a lot of people tried to copy

00:42:16.367 --> 00:42:19.203
some of the things we do,
but they don't understand the—

00:42:20.137 --> 00:42:22.239
you might copy the recipe,
but the sauce ain’t the same.

00:42:22.806 --> 00:42:23.440
You know what I'm saying?

00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:28.045
- [Laughing] Yeah.
- But, um, yeah, I just think different,
and I actually mean that,

00:42:28.045 --> 00:42:31.615
and I move different.
Even the way, the way I dance, you know?

00:42:31.649 --> 00:42:33.651
People understand,
like, I actually move different.

00:42:33.651 --> 00:42:35.753
You know, I'm not, I'm
not the same as everyone else.

00:42:35.753 --> 00:42:38.622
My rhythm,
my timing, my creativity is next level.

00:42:38.923 --> 00:42:40.291
- Mhmm.
- Yeah.
- I love that. OK,

00:42:40.291 --> 00:42:42.593
so most intelligent and most creative.

00:42:42.626 --> 00:42:43.527
- Yeah.
- OK.

00:42:43.527 --> 00:42:45.963
A couple more from me
before we go to fan questions.

00:42:45.963 --> 00:42:48.766
And these are literally—
- Ooh, fan questions. Oh, yeah, we’re live right now. Mwah.
- Yes, we are.

00:42:48.832 --> 00:42:49.900
They're all watching.
- Sup, guys?

00:42:51.101 --> 00:42:53.470
- And this
is just literally because I'm curious.

00:42:53.504 --> 00:42:54.171
- Yeah? OK, here we go.

00:42:54.471 --> 00:42:57.675
- Your first fight
before you were a fighter.

00:42:58.142 --> 00:43:01.979
So, you're fighting, and probably
have no business to be fighting,

00:43:01.979 --> 00:43:03.113
but you're fighting.
- Yeah.

00:43:03.113 --> 00:43:05.249
- What was your first fight
and did you win?
- Before I was a fighter.

00:43:05.983 --> 00:43:08.786
OK. I fought back in Nigeria.

00:43:08.786 --> 00:43:11.255
I definitely had a few scraps.

00:43:11.255 --> 00:43:13.490
But I'm trying to think. OK,
one of my first fights,

00:43:15.025 --> 00:43:16.460
my first fight in New Zealand, right?

00:43:16.460 --> 00:43:19.930
So, what—I've always said this, I didn't know
I was Black till I moved to New Zealand.

00:43:20.164 --> 00:43:22.232
I don't mean that in like the sense
I, you know, my skin tone.

00:43:22.333 --> 00:43:25.202
But I just didn't realize
it was a problem to be Black

00:43:25.769 --> 00:43:28.739
until I was removed from Nigeria,
from the continent of Africa,

00:43:28.739 --> 00:43:30.641
and I was placed in this foreign land

00:43:30.641 --> 00:43:33.043
and people were making fun of me
for my skin tone.
- Mhmm.

00:43:33.611 --> 00:43:35.112
- And they made me feel s--t about it.

00:43:35.112 --> 00:43:36.814
And I was like, “What is it?
What did I do?”

00:43:36.814 --> 00:43:39.249
So this one kid kept on
riding by my house through the weekend

00:43:39.249 --> 00:43:41.318
because he found out
where I live—riding by on his BMX.

00:43:41.685 --> 00:43:43.654
He kept on saying,
“Go back to your country, Blackanese.”

00:43:43.654 --> 00:43:45.022
Funny enough,

00:43:45.022 --> 00:43:46.256
I remember his name.

00:43:46.256 --> 00:43:48.192
And I was just like,
“I don't—I know this kid from school,

00:43:48.192 --> 00:43:50.394
I've seen him around,”
but like, cuz he was giving me s--t at school,

00:43:50.427 --> 00:43:53.764
but I didn't know—like
he was riding by my house.
- Wow.

00:43:53.797 --> 00:43:55.833
- And then—
- Just to bully you?
- Yeah, just talk s--t.

00:43:55.833 --> 00:43:56.867
But then that Monday,

00:43:58.068 --> 00:44:00.971
after
the first interval, he walks up to me

00:44:00.971 --> 00:44:01.438
and goes, “What’s up

00:44:01.438 --> 00:44:04.842
black boy?” Boom, and pushes me.
And he was shorter than me, and I was a short ass

00:44:04.842 --> 00:44:08.579
back then, I was a short ass.
But then I got up and I whooped his ass.

00:44:09.046 --> 00:44:12.883
Threw him towards K Block, beat him up,
threw him to—and I'm crying the whole time.

00:44:12.883 --> 00:44:16.186
I'm beating him up on B Block, K
Block again, and everyone's watching.

00:44:16.186 --> 00:44:18.856
And then one of the teacher stops it,
and I just like, "Leave me alone!”

00:44:19.223 --> 00:44:22.259
And I run away and go hide
somewhere in the field. And, yeah—

00:44:22.259 --> 00:44:24.395
but he definitely never f--k with me
after that again.
- Yeah. [Laughing]

00:44:24.628 --> 00:44:25.696
I'm sure no one did, if you’re just

00:44:25.696 --> 00:44:27.665
throwing him back in.

00:44:27.665 --> 00:44:28.365
- Yeah. Oh no, I threw him, and I’m swinging on him,

00:44:28.365 --> 00:44:31.101
crying and swearing at him
in my, in my language.

00:44:31.568 --> 00:44:33.637
Yeah, it was—I remember that.

00:44:33.637 --> 00:44:34.238
Yeah.

00:44:34.238 --> 00:44:35.973
- Well, cuz to me,
that's the interesting thing

00:44:35.973 --> 00:44:39.209
about being a fighter is I'm like,
there has to be like a point in your life

00:44:39.209 --> 00:44:41.378
where you say,
“Hey, I'd be good at fighting.”

00:44:41.378 --> 00:44:43.647
And I just wonder—
- What point that was?
- Yeah.

00:44:43.647 --> 00:44:48.285
When you know, oh, the thing
I'm good at is f--cking people up.

00:44:48.419 --> 00:44:50.320
- Yeah.
- Like, what is that? [Laughing]

00:44:50.320 --> 00:44:51.622
- The moment I had that—

00:44:51.622 --> 00:44:54.358
so dancing was my, my proper first passion.

00:44:54.358 --> 00:44:56.293
And I always thought like

00:44:56.293 --> 00:45:00.297
I would be on tour with all these guys
and being a backup dancer or a choreographer.

00:45:00.531 --> 00:45:03.000
But then there came a crossroads
in my life where I was like,

00:45:04.101 --> 00:45:06.403
“I'm a great dancer, but

00:45:06.403 --> 00:45:08.939
I'm so good at f--king people up.”

00:45:08.939 --> 00:45:11.241
I'm like, “But I can always dance,

00:45:12.076 --> 00:45:15.245
but I may end up in jail
if I keep just f--king people up randomly.”

00:45:15.245 --> 00:45:16.814
So I decided to take this as a career.

00:45:16.814 --> 00:45:17.681
So that was a crossroads.

00:45:17.681 --> 00:45:21.719
But, yeah, I think just watching
greats like Anderson

00:45:21.719 --> 00:45:25.889
Silva, Muhammad Ali, Prince Naseem,
and all of a sudden, “You know what?

00:45:26.090 --> 00:45:27.791
This is my—this the path I'm going to take.”

00:45:27.791 --> 00:45:29.359
- Yeah. How,

00:45:29.359 --> 00:45:32.763
if you were describing it
to somebody in great detail...
- Mhmm.

00:45:33.597 --> 00:45:36.066
- how does it feel to punch someone?
- Oh.

00:45:36.433 --> 00:45:38.736
- And how does it feel to be punched?

00:45:38.736 --> 00:45:42.239
- Being punched doesn't actually hurt
like you think, cuz adrenaline's going.

00:45:42.673 --> 00:45:46.210
And it only if it, if it rattles
your brain, then you can get rocked.

00:45:46.210 --> 00:45:49.346
Or if it shuts you off,
you get knocked out. But being punched,

00:45:49.580 --> 00:45:50.914
I don't fear being punched.

00:45:50.914 --> 00:45:52.382
You know, I don't like being punched.

00:45:53.784 --> 00:45:55.385
Nah, but um—

00:45:55.385 --> 00:45:56.186
Yeah. At least there’s—

00:45:56.320 --> 00:45:57.254
- But punching someone.

00:45:57.254 --> 00:45:59.757
- Yeah, punching someone,

00:46:00.124 --> 00:46:01.091
knocking someone out,

00:46:01.091 --> 00:46:03.160
sometimes it's the punch

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:04.828
you don't really try
and knock them out with that

00:46:04.828 --> 00:46:07.598
just turns them off, and you’d be surprised.
It feels like nothing.

00:46:07.598 --> 00:46:10.467
It feels like you're punching through air
sometimes.

00:46:10.934 --> 00:46:12.970
Yeah. But then—I'm trying to think.

00:46:12.970 --> 00:46:14.071
Example, the Whittaker shot.

00:46:14.071 --> 00:46:16.640
When I cracked him—boom.

00:46:16.640 --> 00:46:18.208
That one,

00:46:18.742 --> 00:46:20.310
It felt like I just went through him.

00:46:20.310 --> 00:46:24.948
Same with Costa, like, I like—
I slipped a jab, he threw the left hook,

00:46:24.948 --> 00:46:27.284
and I cracked him with the left hook
and just felt like I went through them.

00:46:27.518 --> 00:46:28.752
- Yeah.
- Yeah. It just felt like nothing.

00:46:28.752 --> 00:46:30.521
So it feels like you're punching
through nothing.

00:46:30.521 --> 00:46:31.288
- OK.
- Yeah.

00:46:31.288 --> 00:46:34.024
- No. OK. I'm visualizing it again—
- Because you hit ‘em, you feel it, you get the—

00:46:34.024 --> 00:46:37.828
- Because, like, I doubt I'm ever gonna knock someone out,
so I want to know what it's actually like.

00:46:37.861 --> 00:46:39.763
- Yeah. You feel the impact, but it just feels like nothing really.

00:46:39.763 --> 00:46:40.998
Yeah.
- Yeah, OK.

00:46:40.998 --> 00:46:44.101
All right, so before we get to fan
questions, I do want to ask you about

00:46:44.101 --> 00:46:46.270
working with Paradigm.
- Oh my Gs.
- Because I think it's so cool

00:46:46.270 --> 00:46:49.473
that you all like—
- GP.
- Yeah, like you rep so many other champions.

00:46:49.473 --> 00:46:52.109
So what is that experience been like?

00:46:52.109 --> 00:46:55.145
- Yeah, well Paradigm, I'm glad I brought them on
because I felt like they were

00:46:55.145 --> 00:46:58.048
the guys to get me to that next level.

00:46:58.382 --> 00:47:01.185
You know, when it comes to, I guess,

00:47:01.185 --> 00:47:05.022
dealing with the
media stuff, the promotion,

00:47:06.056 --> 00:47:07.157
sponsorships,

00:47:07.157 --> 00:47:10.394
endorsements and the pay, cuz,
you know,

00:47:10.394 --> 00:47:13.497
they've had, they have,
what's his name, Conor on the team as well.

00:47:13.497 --> 00:47:16.800
So he's the highest paid UFC fighter.
Now because of Paradigm,

00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:19.002
I'm the second-highest paid UFC fighter.

00:47:19.002 --> 00:47:22.306
- That’s fire.
- And, yeah, I'm,
I'm still greedy because I know my worth.

00:47:22.472 --> 00:47:23.740
So I want more.

00:47:23.740 --> 00:47:26.076
And I know what's been left on the table
and I want to take some more.

00:47:26.143 --> 00:47:26.543
- Yeah.

00:47:26.543 --> 00:47:29.146
- And also they're helping me
as well in certain aspects to

00:47:29.980 --> 00:47:33.083
make sure that the fighters
on the roster as well get some.

00:47:33.083 --> 00:47:35.352
But it's not an easy process.
It's just, it's a lengthy process.

00:47:35.352 --> 00:47:37.688
But right now,
I'm grateful for the position I'm in.

00:47:37.688 --> 00:47:41.158
And thanks to my people at Paradigm.
A special shout out to Tim.

00:47:41.158 --> 00:47:42.993
- Special shout out to Tim.

00:47:42.993 --> 00:47:44.228
- Tim, he's my, he’s my boy.

00:47:44.228 --> 00:47:45.996
So, yeah, special shout out to him as well.

00:47:45.996 --> 00:47:46.530
- OK.

00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:47.931
I love that. Shout out to Paradigm.

00:47:47.931 --> 00:47:50.267
All right, Rocky. Fan questions?

00:47:50.267 --> 00:47:53.337
- [Producer:] What do you think Pereira will
bring out of you that other fighters haven’t?

00:47:54.238 --> 00:47:56.106
- Pereira, what would he bring out of me?

00:47:56.106 --> 00:47:59.409
He's not gonna shy away,
because he already has that in his mind

00:47:59.409 --> 00:48:01.144
that he thinks I'm easy
because he's beat me.

00:48:01.144 --> 00:48:03.547
So he's not going to shy away. He's
going to actually try and attack me.

00:48:03.547 --> 00:48:06.817
I'm going to try to win the fight,
which always brings out the best in me.

00:48:06.817 --> 00:48:09.486
When someone tries to fight,
you know, I'm a fighter.

00:48:09.486 --> 00:48:12.089
I'm right there trying to fight.
But then when someone's trying to be—

00:48:14.091 --> 00:48:16.960
uh, they’re trying to survive,
it makes it harder to take them away.

00:48:16.960 --> 00:48:18.929
So, I'm glad
this guy's not going to try to survive.

00:48:18.929 --> 00:48:20.864
He's going to try and win. Yeah.

00:48:20.864 --> 00:48:22.366
So I'm going to take that away from him.

00:48:22.366 --> 00:48:24.601
- OK, I like that. Another one?

00:48:24.601 --> 00:48:26.670
- [Producer:] What round are you knocking him out?

00:48:26.670 --> 00:48:28.238
- I can't tell you that.

00:48:28.238 --> 00:48:31.241
Like I said, I'm saying
less this whole lead up to this fight.

00:48:32.576 --> 00:48:33.744
I just—you know what?

00:48:33.744 --> 00:48:35.412
Like I said,
I might not even knock him out.

00:48:35.412 --> 00:48:39.983
I might literally just f--king jab,
leg kick and just move out the way

00:48:40.017 --> 00:48:41.218
and then get a decision-win.

00:48:41.218 --> 00:48:43.420
But, hey, stay tuned.

00:48:43.420 --> 00:48:44.788
Or I might get knocked out.

00:48:44.788 --> 00:48:47.157
Stay tuned. You might find out.

00:48:47.157 --> 00:48:50.193
- I would say, I respect that
because it's hard to say

00:48:50.193 --> 00:48:52.663
less, like being silent is difficult.

00:48:52.663 --> 00:48:54.631
- Trust me, and for me in this position,

00:48:54.631 --> 00:48:58.802
like I said, the duality—when
I'm by myself, my people know me,

00:48:58.802 --> 00:49:01.438
I chill, I barely say a word,
and we can talk for hours, but now I’ll

00:49:01.438 --> 00:49:03.674
spend hours just chilling, saying less.

00:49:03.674 --> 00:49:05.575
But when it’s this, I'm a social butterfly.

00:49:05.575 --> 00:49:10.113
I can rap, but for me, I just—silence,
say less, say less.

00:49:10.113 --> 00:49:11.882
This camp, I'm just like, “Yo, just chill.”

00:49:11.882 --> 00:49:13.917
Let him, let him do all the talking.

00:49:13.917 --> 00:49:16.887
I'll do my talking
when it's time in the Octagon.
- Nice. Any more?

00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:18.455
- [Producer:] OK, this one’s a two-part.

00:49:18.455 --> 00:49:23.160
What—do you have any crazy weight-cutting
stories, and what's your favorite meal after you’re done?
- Ooh.

00:49:23.827 --> 00:49:26.330
- Yeah, what's

00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:30.167
the craziest thing
that you have done to make weight?

00:49:30.300 --> 00:49:31.034
So cutting weight.

00:49:37.507 --> 00:49:39.142
- [Laughing] Ah, you don't know Tim. But I’m like...

00:49:40.043 --> 00:49:42.045
let me pause, pause, pause let me think

00:49:42.045 --> 00:49:43.947
if I can say this.
- No, you already have it.

00:49:43.947 --> 00:49:47.617
You have to tell us, those are the rules.

00:49:47.651 --> 00:49:54.491
Ahh, man. [Lips smacking]

00:49:54.825 --> 00:49:58.328
It’s just, ahh, I...

00:49:58.328 --> 00:50:00.897
ah, f--k, hold up. F--king hell. [Laughing]

00:50:00.897 --> 00:50:04.234
- OK, all this but—you know,
you have to tell us. Like, you can't,

00:50:04.301 --> 00:50:06.570
you can't do this pause.
- Oh man, I know, I was trying to—

00:50:06.603 --> 00:50:09.139
- I feel like I know so much about you now.
- Yeah! [Laughing]

00:50:09.139 --> 00:50:11.174
- What is the crazy thing you did?

00:50:12.109 --> 00:50:15.612
- I was trying to—well, back in kickboxing,
back in the day, when I was an amateur,

00:50:15.612 --> 00:50:18.849
when I was really young and had no—
I didn't have the fight dietician,

00:50:18.849 --> 00:50:21.084
who was the guy that looks after us here
with my meals and whatnot,

00:50:21.084 --> 00:50:23.053
I did not have him on deck.

00:50:23.053 --> 00:50:26.056
I wasn't in the UFC.

00:50:26.056 --> 00:50:27.224
Oh, f--k man. [Laughing]

00:50:28.325 --> 00:50:29.593
OK, I erm...

00:50:31.194 --> 00:50:33.497
f—k, how do put this?

00:50:33.497 --> 00:50:35.766
I busted a nut to make weight.
[Both laughing]

00:50:39.302 --> 00:50:42.105
- OK, rewind.

00:50:42.205 --> 00:50:43.473
- Let's not go into that story, but that's just...

00:50:43.473 --> 00:50:45.909
- No, I'm not going to ask the specifics of that part.
[Adesanya laughing]

00:50:45.909 --> 00:50:49.246
But how much does that weigh? I mean...

00:50:50.047 --> 00:50:51.982
- You really wanted to know?

00:50:52.082 --> 00:50:52.449
- No! I guess,

00:50:52.449 --> 00:50:55.052
I'm just like I would never think,
“Oh, this is the thing

00:50:55.285 --> 00:50:55.619
to do.”

00:50:55.619 --> 00:51:00.490
- So, at the time, I was young,
and I was on that whole no...before a fight. And da, da, da, da.

00:51:00.490 --> 00:51:03.260
Before I knew it was a myth.

00:51:03.260 --> 00:51:06.096
And, yeah, I just—

00:51:06.096 --> 00:51:09.332
and then the few grams came off.
100 grams.

00:51:09.466 --> 00:51:10.867
- You made weight.
- Yeah, I made weight [Laughing]

00:51:10.867 --> 00:51:15.539
- Wow. This is the lesson of today,
fighters.

00:51:16.406 --> 00:51:17.207
- Exclusive! But I wouldn't advise it.

00:51:17.207 --> 00:51:20.177
Ey, I was younger back
then. Like, 21, 22.

00:51:20.544 --> 00:51:22.679
I didn't know what I was doing
with weight cutting.

00:51:23.313 --> 00:51:26.483
And, yeah, that was, er...yeah,
that was something.

00:51:26.850 --> 00:51:29.219
- But you made weight.
- I made weight.
I've never missed weight in my life.

00:51:29.252 --> 00:51:30.520
- Look at that.

00:51:30.520 --> 00:51:33.457
- Knock on wood I never will.
- What do you think is the lesson in that
in that story?

00:51:33.523 --> 00:51:35.258
- Well, I wouldn't advise it. I would—

00:51:35.258 --> 00:51:38.628
the lesson is just get a proper
dietician and,

00:51:38.628 --> 00:51:41.998
you know, and learn how to water load,
get your nutrition right,

00:51:41.998 --> 00:51:46.636
so you can make weight without,
you know, doing your thing.

00:51:47.604 --> 00:51:48.238
-  [Laughing] I love it.
- F--k.

00:51:48.238 --> 00:51:51.208
